        }


        [PexMethod]
        public void PUT_SetContract_Test(ArrayList arrList, int x, int index)
        {
            PUT_SetContract(arrList, x, index);
        }
    }
}

```


## 使用方法

在需要添加测试用例的方法上添加PexMethod特性，然后在该方法中添加一个副本方法，该方法名前缀为PUT_，参数为[PexAssumeUnderTest]，最后调用副本方法。


## Reference

[PexMethod] 特性用于指明一个方法是可以被Pex运行器测试的方法。
[PexAssumeUnderTest] 属性用于指定应该在该方法执行的过程中，对一个方法进行测试。通常用于在该方法执行之前假设一个方法，然后在执行该方法时测试该方法的行为。

[PexMethod]：标记方法为Pex应该测试的。
[PexAssumeUnderTest]：标记参数为一个方法。

[PexObserve] 用于观测某些值的变化并打印出来。
PexObserve.ValueForViewing 打印出值。

更多信息可以参考 https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/dn363916.aspx

## Note

这只是一个可能的情况，具体的使用方法和效果需要看具体的情况和需要测试的源代码。

参考资料：[PexMethod] 特性用于指明一个方法是可以被Pex运行器测试, [PexAssumeUnderTest] 属性用于指定应该在该方法执行的过程中, 然后在执行该方法时测试该方法的行为。

[PexObserve] 用于观测某些值的变化并打印出来。 PexObserve.ValueForViewing 打印出值。

更多信息可以参考：[https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/dn363916.aspx:title]---
layout: post
title: "Spatial Indexing Structures"
date: 2019-01-24 15:50:22 +0530
tags: [spatial-indexing, geometry, databases, sql]
---

Spatial indexes are a critical part of spatial databases. They are used to quickly locate information related to a spatial feature, such as maps, images, or geospatial points. Spatial Indexes can significantly speed up spatial queries on data, allowing for efficient retrieval of spatial objects.

Types of spatial index structures can be broadly classified into two categories:

1. **Geometry-Based Indexes**: In geometry-based indexes, data is indexed based on its geometric properties. 

  * **R-tree**: An R-tree is a type of spatial index which is a space-filling data structure for organizing and storing spatial objects in memory. R-trees are most suitable for multi-dimensional spatial data.

  * **Quadtree**: Unlike other tree structures, a Quadtree doesn't split items into different categories (as in a B-tree or KD-tree). Instead, it splits the space into four equal regions and stores only the objects that could fall into these regions.

  * **KD-tree**: K-D tree is a binary space partitioning data structure for organizing points in a k-dimensional space. Kd-tree is useful for applications like nearest neighbor searches and range searching.

2. **Attribute-Based Indexes**: Attribute-based spatial indexes also use attributes or values associated with the spatial objects to build the index. 

  * **Grid Index**: A grid index structure organizes all the feature points in a grid system. Each cell in the grid usually has a fixed size and can hold a maximum of a few hundred feature points.

  * **Loose Index**: A loose index structure allows for the insertion--------------------	    // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ index of x in new array list is greater than or equal to position where it is set
            // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ arrList.Contains\(x\) will be true after setting new value

        }
    }
